<html xmlns:o='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:office' xmlns:w='urn:schemas-microsoft-com:office:word' xmlns='http://www.w3.org/TR/REC-html40'>
<head><meta charset='utf-8'><title>Mathematics Unit Test</title>
<style>
body { font-family: 'Times New Roman', serif; font-size: 12pt; line-height: 1.4; margin: 20px; }
.header { text-align: center; font-weight: bold; margin-bottom: 20px; border-bottom: 2px solid #000; padding-bottom: 10px; }
</style>
</head>
<body>
<div class='header'>
    <h2>RRB Group of Schools</h2>
    <h3>Unit Test — Mathematics (Class 10 A)</h3>
</div>
<table width='100%' style='margin-bottom:15px;font-weight:bold;'>
    <tr>
        <td>Time Allowed: 1 Hour</td>
        <td align='right'>Maximum Marks: 25</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
        <td>Teacher: GAURAV SHUKLA</td>
        <td align='right'>Date: 21/08/2026</td>
    </tr>
</table>
<hr>
<h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section A: Multiple Choice Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Choose the correct option for each of the following questions.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q1.</strong> The distance of the point P(-6, 8) from the origin is:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) 8 units</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) 2&radic;<span style="border-top:1px solid #000;padding-top:1px;margin-left:1px;">7</span> units</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) 10 units</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) 6 units</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q2.</strong> If the distance between the points (4, p) and (1, 0) is 5 units, the value of p can be:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) 4 only</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) -4 only</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) &plusmn; 4</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) 0</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q3.</strong> The coordinates of the point which divides the line segment joining the points (a, b) and (a, -b) in the ratio 1:2 internally are:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) (a, <span style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:-0.4em;text-align:center;margin:0 2px;"><span style="border-bottom:1px solid #000;display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">b</span><span style="display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">3</span></span>)</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) (a, -<span style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:-0.4em;text-align:center;margin:0 2px;"><span style="border-bottom:1px solid #000;display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">b</span><span style="display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">3</span></span>)</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) (a, <span style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:-0.4em;text-align:center;margin:0 2px;"><span style="border-bottom:1px solid #000;display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">2b</span><span style="display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">3</span></span>)</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) (<span style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:-0.4em;text-align:center;margin:0 2px;"><span style="border-bottom:1px solid #000;display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">a</span><span style="display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">3</span></span>, <span style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:-0.4em;text-align:center;margin:0 2px;"><span style="border-bottom:1px solid #000;display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">b</span><span style="display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">3</span></span>)</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q4.</strong> The centroid of the triangle whose vertices are (3, -5), (-7, 4), and (10, -2) is:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) (2, -1)</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) (1, -1)</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) (-1, 1)</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) (2, 1)</li></ul><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q5.</strong> If the points A(1, 2), B(0, 0), and C(a, b) are collinear, then:</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) 2a = b</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) a = b</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) a = 2b</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) a + b = 0</li></ul><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section B: Fill in the Blanks</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Fill in the blanks with appropriate answers.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q6.</strong> The point on the x-axis which is equidistant from (2, -5) and (-2, 9) is _______.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q7.</strong> The area of a triangle formed by the points (x1, y1), (x2, y2), and (x3, y3) is zero if the points are _______.</div><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section C: Assertion-Reason</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Direction: In question number 8, a statement of Assertion (A) is followed by a statement of Reason (R). Choose the correct option.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q8.</strong> Assertion (A): The point (-1, 6) divides the line segment joining the points (-3, 10) and (6, -8) in the ratio 2:7 internally.
Reason (R): The coordinates of the point P(x, y) which divides the line segment joining P<sub>1</sub>(x<sub>1</sub>, y<sub>1</sub>) and P<sub>2</sub>(x<sub>2</sub>, y<sub>2</sub>) in the ratio m<sub>1</sub>:m<sub>2</sub> are given by (<span style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:-0.4em;text-align:center;margin:0 2px;"><span style="border-bottom:1px solid #000;display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">m<sub>1</sub>x<sub>2</sub> + m<sub>2</sub>x<sub>1</sub></span><span style="display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">m<sub>1</sub> + m<sub>2</sub></span></span>, <span style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:-0.4em;text-align:center;margin:0 2px;"><span style="border-bottom:1px solid #000;display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">m<sub>1</sub>y<sub>2</sub> + m<sub>2</sub>y<sub>1</sub></span><span style="display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">m<sub>1</sub> + m<sub>2</sub></span></span>).</div><ul style='list-style-type:none;padding-left:15px;margin-top:4px;'><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(a) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true and Reason (R) is the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(b) Both Assertion (A) and Reason (R) are true but Reason (R) is not the correct explanation of Assertion (A).</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(c) Assertion (A) is true but Reason (R) is false.</li><li style='margin-bottom:2px;'>(d) Assertion (A) is false but Reason (R) is true.</li></ul><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section D: Very Short Answer Type Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Answer the following questions.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q9.</strong> Find the coordinates of the point which divides the join of (-1, 7) and (4, -3) in the ratio 2:3.</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q10.</strong> Find the relation between x and y such that the point (x, y) is equidistant from the points (3, 6) and (-3, 4).</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q11.</strong> Determine if the points (1, 5), (2, 3), and (-2, -11) are collinear.</div><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section E: Short Answer Type Questions</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Answer the following questions.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q12.</strong> Find the area of the rhombus if its vertices are (3, 0), (4, 5), (-1, 4), and (-2, -1) taken in order. [Hint: Area of a rhombus = <span style="display:inline-block;vertical-align:-0.4em;text-align:center;margin:0 2px;"><span style="border-bottom:1px solid #000;display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">1</span><span style="display:block;padding:0 2px;font-size:0.9em;">2</span></span> (product of diagonals)]</div><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q13.</strong> If A(-5, 7), B(-4, -5), C(-1, -6) and D(4, 5) are the vertices of a quadrilateral, find the area of the quadrilateral ABCD.</div><h3 style='margin-top:16px;color:#1e1b4b;border-bottom:1px solid #ddd;'>Section F: Long Answer Type Question</h3><p style='font-style:italic;color:#555;'>Note: Answer the following question in detail.</p><div style='margin-bottom:10px;'><strong>Q14.</strong> Points A(-1, y) and B(5, 7) lie on a circle with centre O(2, -3y). Find the values of y. Hence, find the radius of the circle.</div>
</body>
</html>